      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many unused helper methods, unused imports, and lacks clarity about why an empty token appears. I'll write a cleaner version.Now I'll compile-check the test.The improved test compiles successfully (`COMPILE_OK`). The refactored version removes all unused imports, constants, and helper methods, renames `tok` to `tokenizer` for clarity, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining why a double space in the input produces an empty token — making the test's intent immediately clear to future readers."
